&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Nebius:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nebius is leading a new era in cloud infrastructure for the global AI economy. We are building a full-stack AI cloud platform that supports developers and enterprises from data and model training through to production deployment, without the cost and complexity of building large in-house AI/ML infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Built by engineers, for engineers. From large-scale GPU orchestration to inference optimization, we own the hard problems across compute, storage, networking and applied AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Listed on Nasdaq (NBIS) and headquartered in Amsterdam, we have a global footprint with R&amp;amp;D hubs across Europe, the UK, North America and Israel. Our team of 1,500+ includes hundreds of engineers with deep expertise across hardware, software and AI R&amp;amp;D.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;The role:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;Nebius is building the cloud infrastructure that will power the next generation of Physical AI—robotics, autonomous systems, simulation, and embodied intelligence operating in the real world. As a European-headquartered AI infrastructure company, EMEA is a strategic home market for Nebius and one of the most consequential regions in the global Physical AI buildout—from UK autonomy and foundation-model players, to German humanoid and industrial robotics, to Swiss legged-robotics and Israeli/Nordic frontier startups, to the EU&#39;s rapidly accelerating defence and dual-use AI ecosystem.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;The Principal, EMEA GTM – Physical AI owns our GTM motion across EMEA: a regional sales overlay role built to drive repeatable revenue within our first and most important segment—Physical AI natives based in or operating across Europe, the Middle East, and Africa. This is not a generalist regional AE seat. It is a domain-led, EMEA-anchored pipeline generator and deal accelerator designed to create leverage: tighter narratives, sharper use-case framing, and category assets that the EMEA field can run independently.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;You will open strategic, executive-level accounts across the EMEA Physical AI ecosystem, generate qualified pipeline, and personally lead engagement across our EMEA Top 25 target list. On top-tier deals, you will partner directly with EMEA Account Executives, regional sales leadership, and the Physical AI Field CTO team to shape the opportunity early, act as executive sponsor, and accelerate time-to-close. In parallel, you will turn what you learn in-region into repeatable motions—subsegment theses, playbooks, and enablement—tailored to the EMEA buyer, the regulatory environment (EU AI Act, GDPR, data sovereignty), and the region&#39;s multi-country go-to-market complexity.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;This is a definitive “zero-to-one” opportunity to build the EMEA commercial foundation for a new cloud category from the ground up, in a region where Nebius has structural home-market advantage. You are welcome to work remotely from within EMEA, with strong preference for London or Munich; Paris or Amsterdam are also viable.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Strong&quot;&gt;Your responsibilities will include:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EMEA Pipeline Generation &amp;amp; Account Ownership:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Generate qualified, industry-sourced pipeline and open strategic, executive-level accounts within the EMEA Physical AI ecosystem—autonomous vehicles, humanoid and industrial robotics, foundation-model and world-model builders, industrial computer vision, and the OEM/Tier-1 cohort investing in Physical AI in Germany, France, Sweden, and Italy. Personally own engagement for our EMEA Top 25 target list and ensure each account has a clear engagement plan and is actively progressing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deal Acceleration with the&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EMEA Field:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Frame use cases and shape solution direction in the early stages of a deal. Partner directly with EMEA AEs, regional GMs, and the Field CTO on top-tier accounts to accelerate closure, acting as the executive sponsor and regional domain authority. Your involvement is the difference between a stalled deal and a closed one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EMEA Lighthouse Account Execution:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Identify and secure the most innovative companies across EMEA&#39;s AI-native Physical AI segments—autonomy, humanoid robotics, foundation/world-model builders, simulation-first startups, defense and dual-use—converting them into flagship customer wins that validate our platform, establish category credibility in-region, and create reference gravity for the rest of EMEA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Subsegment Theses &amp;amp; Category Building (EMEA Lens):&lt;/strong&gt; Define EMEA-specific subsegment theses and extract cross-account insights to establish repeatable deal patterns. Identify which European customer profiles convert fastest, which use cases generate the highest consumption, which objections appear most frequently (sovereignty, AI Act compliance, data residency, EU-based support), and which regional GTM motions actually work. Operationalize those learnings into scalable sales plays the EMEA field can run.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EMEA Sales Playbook Development:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Codify market learnings into a comprehensive “EMEA Physical AI Playbook.” Develop battle cards, positioning guides, objection-handling frameworks, and competitive intelligence materials specific to the EMEA buyer. Deliver formalized, documented sales motions that the broader EMEA field team—across the UK, DACH, France, Benelux, Nordics, Southern Europe, the Middle East, and Israel—can execute independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regional Field Enablement:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as a force multiplier for the EMEA sales organization. Run internal enablement sessions and training for EMEA Sales, SAs, and Marketing on Physical AI positioning, target personas, regional regulatory framing (EU AI Act, GDPR, sovereignty), and use-case framing. Publish case studies and reference stories from EMEA lighthouse wins to arm the broader regional team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Revenue Conversion in Region:&lt;/strong&gt; Own the long-term revenue trajectory of the Physical AI domain in EMEA, ensuring that early lighthouse technical wins translate into high-volume compute consumption as customers scale their training, simulation, and inference workloads on Nebius infrastructure—and that EMEA contributes its full share of the Physical AI revenue target.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;E&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MEA Market Intelligence &amp;amp; Competitive Positioning:&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain a real-time understanding of the EMEA Physical AI competitive landscape. Track where other cloud providers are winning or losing within our target segments. Feed competitive intelligence into sales assets and deal strategy. Position Nebius&#39;s European-headquartered, sovereignty-friendly posture as a structural advantage where it matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regional Ecosystem Evangelism:&lt;/strong&gt; Evangelize our capabilities at EMEA-relevant industry events (e.g., Hannover Messe, Automatica, European Robotics Forum, VivaTech, AI Summit London, Web Summit, Slush, and EMEA editions of ICRA/IROS/CoRL when applicable) and customer executive briefings—positioning Nebius as the infrastructure of choice for Physical AI workloads built and deployed in Europe and across the broader EMEA region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Strong&quot;&gt;We expect you to have:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;7+ years &lt;/strong&gt;of experience in sales overlay, GTM strategy, or domain-specialist selling within Cloud, AI Infrastructure, or High-Performance Computing—with a meaningful portion of that experience focused on EMEA customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EMEA Operating Fluency: &lt;/strong&gt;Deep familiarity with how to sell across the UK, DACH, France, Benelux, Nordics, Southern Europe, the Middle East, and Israel. You understand that EMEA is not one market and you have a point of view on which subregions to lead with for a category like Physical AI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proven Pipeline Generation: &lt;/strong&gt;Demonstrated track record of personally sourcing and generating qualified pipeline across EMEA through outbound prospecting, industry relationships, and strategic account engagement at the executive level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deal Acceleration DNA: &lt;/strong&gt;Experience partnering with Account Executives across multiple EMEA countries to accelerate complex enterprise and startup deals. You know how to frame a use case, position value, and act as an executive sponsor to drive closure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sales Playbook Builder: &lt;/strong&gt;You have built GTM motions from scratch before—segmenting a market, defining the pitch, creating the sales plays, and training a broader regional team to execute. Bonus if you have done it specifically for EMEA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deep Domain Fluency: &lt;/strong&gt;You speak the language of the builders. You understand the difference between model training, simulation, synthetic data generation, and inference workloads. You know the key players—startups and incumbents—across the modern Physical AI stack, with strong recall of the European cohort specifically.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regulatory &amp;amp; Sovereignty Awareness: &lt;/strong&gt;Working knowledge of the EU AI Act, GDPR, data-residency expectations, and the sovereign-cloud conversation in Europe. You can speak credibly with customers for whom these are first-order procurement considerations rather than afterthoughts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enablement Mindset: &lt;/strong&gt;You enjoy teaching and scaling knowledge. You can take complex technical wins and distill them into simple, repeatable sales motions for a broader EMEA team that lacks your domain depth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Orchestration: &lt;/strong&gt;Proven track record of working across Sales, SAs, Marketing, and Product Marketing—often across multiple EMEA countries and time zones—to align distinct teams behind a unified GTM execution plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Startup &amp;amp; AI-Native Fluency: &lt;/strong&gt;Experience working with (or selling to) high-growth, venture-backed European startups. You understand the urgency, the technical depth, and the rapid decision-making of this customer base, as well as how European founders and CTOs evaluate infrastructure differently from their US counterparts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication: &lt;/strong&gt;Strong executive presence and communication skills, capable of holding your own with VC-backed founders, CTOs, and senior technical decision-makers across EMEA. Additional European languages (German, French) are a plus, not a requirement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comfort in Ambiguity: &lt;/strong&gt;Experience operating in fast-moving environments where the sales motion is not yet fully defined and requires real-time iteration and pattern recognition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Strong&quot;&gt;Why Nebius:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regional Ownership: &lt;/strong&gt;You are not inheriting a quota on an existing product line in an existing region; you are building the EMEA revenue engine for an entirely new category of cloud infrastructure, in our strategic home market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Category Definition: &lt;/strong&gt;Define the EMEA playbook that the rest of the company will use to sell Physical AI in the region for years to come.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Frontier Technology: &lt;/strong&gt;Work at the bleeding edge of embodied intelligence, engaging with the companies defining the future of robotics, autonomy, and the physical world—right at the center of Europe&#39;s accelerating AI buildout.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Structural Advantage: &lt;/strong&gt;Nebius is European-headquartered. Sovereignty, EU data residency, and regulatory alignment are real selling points—not retrofits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;High Leverage: &lt;/strong&gt;Focus on the top 10% of transformative EMEA customers that drive the next 90% of growth within this segment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mission: &lt;/strong&gt;Help define how intelligence moves from the data center into the physical world—starting from Europe. &lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;#LI-GH1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits &amp;amp; Perks:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Career growth and learning opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility and ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative and innovative culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to work on impactful AI projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;International environment and talented teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What&#39;s it like to work at Nebius:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fast moving&amp;nbsp;- Bold thinking&amp;nbsp;- Constant growth&amp;nbsp;- Meaningful impact&amp;nbsp;- Trust and real ownership&amp;nbsp;- Opportunity to shape the future of AI&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nebius is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and diverse workplace and to providing equal employment opportunities in all aspects of employment. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), national origin, ancestry, age, disability, genetic information, marital status, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants must be authorized to work in the country in which they apply and will be required to provide proof of employment eligibility as a condition of hire.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you need accommodations during the application process, please let us know.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Verve has created a more efficient and privacy-focused way to buy and monetize advertising. Verve is an ecosystem of demand and supply technologies fusing data, media, and technology together to deliver results and growth to both advertisers and publishers–no matter the screen or location, no matter who, what, or where a customer is. With 30 offices across the globe and with an eye on servicing forward-thinking advertising customers, Verve’s solutions are trusted by more than 90 of the United States’ top 100 advertisers, 4,000 publishers globally, and the world’s top demand-side platforms. Learn more at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://verve.com/&quot;&gt;verve.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Position&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role drives the strategic expansion of supply, demand, and data partnerships across Verve and all business lines. Sitting at the intersection of Business Development, Product, and Operations, you will source and negotiate high-impact agreements, deepen strategic accounts, and collaborate with Sales Engineering and Product to prioritize integrations that move the needle. As a build-and-own role, success is measured by the partnerships you source and close, the top-line revenue they unlock, and their operational performance post-launch.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Market Intelligence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track programmatic, in-app, web, and CTV trends to anticipate shifts in supply and demand economics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify white-space partnership opportunities and deliver data-backed recommendations to guide company’s strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor competitive dynamics, pricing, and deal structures to maintain Verve’s market edge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share actionable market intelligence with Product, Sales, and Leadership to shape GTM and product roadmaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partnerships Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, prioritize, and secure high-impact demand, supply, and data partnerships to maximize liquidity and expand market reach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate market-competitive commercial agreements across key pricing, revenue, and exclusivity frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the partner lifecycle from initial sourcing through live integration, collaborating cross-functionally to ensure rapid deployment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead executive partner relationships to gather performance insights, mitigate operational risks, and unlock strategic expansion opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance Analytics &amp;amp; Operations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track key metrics, including fill rates, yield, latency, and quality, to continuously optimize portfolio health, diagnose underperformance, and execute cross-functional corrective action plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate market needs into product requirements, collaborating with Product, Engineering, and Finance on roadmaps, deal economics, and forecasting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver executive reporting and business reviews on portfolio performance, revenue health, and strategic growth drivers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Govern end-to-end partnership operational flows, ensuring full alignment with corporate compliance frameworks, risk policies, and SLA standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deliver Revenue Growth:&lt;/strong&gt; Source and close supply, demand, and data deals that expand marketplace liquidity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accelerate Time-to-Live:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead end-to-end onboarding cross-functionally to convert signed contracts into live, optimized traffic in a timely and efficient manner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Maximize Portfolio Yield:&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain strong account health by continuously tuning fill rates and resolving performance bottlenecks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Guide Strategy with Intel: &lt;/strong&gt;Translate competitive dynamics and market trends into actionable inputs for Product, Sales, and Leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5-8+ years of business development, partnerships, or strategic account management in ad tech, programmatic, or mobile advertising (e.g., Partner Manager, BD Manager, Strategic Partnerships Manager).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven cross-functional collaborator, skilled at driving alignment across Engineering, Product, Ops, Legal, and Finance to navigate ambiguity, streamline workflows, and execute complex product launches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established network and active relationships with SSPs, DSPs, or major publishers across mobile, CTV, or in-app ecosystems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of sourcing, negotiating, and closing end-to-end commercial agreements, owning deal terms and financial modeling rather than solely relationship management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep technical proficiency in SSP/DSP mechanics, OpenRTB specifications, header bidding, yield optimization, and ad server integration QA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to bridge technical and commercial teams, translating complex engineering and product concepts into accessible, business-driven insights for non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional executive communication skills, with a track record of articulating strategy, deal economics, and complex operational performance to senior leadership and C-suite executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;Verve provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If you are a California resident subject to the California Consumer Privacy Act, &lt;a href=&quot;https://verve.com/california-applicant-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;click here&lt;/a&gt; to understand how Verve processes your personal information and how you can exercise your rights.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;If you are located in the EU or UK visit our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot; href=&quot;https://verve.com/applicant-privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;privacy policy&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt; to understand how Verve processes your personal information and how you can exercise your rights.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About WPP Media&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;WPP is the trusted growth partner for the world’s leading brands. With exceptional talent, trusted data and intelligence, and world-class partnerships – all united by our pioneering agentic marketing platform, WPP Open – we help clients navigate change, capture opportunity, and deliver transformational growth. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;WPP Media is WPP&#39;s AI-driven media operating unit, bringing together media, data, and partnerships to deliver creative personalisation at scale. Connected through WPP Open and powered by Open Intelligence, clients see exactly where, how, and why their media investment is working.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For more information, visit &lt;a href=&quot;wppmedia.com&quot;&gt;wppmedia.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1772 - Lead Software Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Summary and Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Code, we design and build digital products and platforms for a range of clients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Lead Software Engineer who wants to stay hands-on. You’ll write production code, make and shape technical decisions, and support a small group of engineers.&lt;br&gt;This isn’t a role where you step away from engineering to manage from the side lines. You’ll be involved in the day-to-day work: thinking through architecture, reviewing code, tackling difficult problems and helping the team find sensible ways forward when things get complicated.&lt;br&gt;You’ll line manage 3–4 engineers, with regular 1:1s and responsibility for supporting their development. A big part of the role is helping other engineers get better at what they do — not by having all the answers, but by giving them the support and technical direction they need.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;You’ll work closely with delivery managers, designers, product managers, principal engineers and clients. Sometimes that means working through a difficult technical problem; sometimes it means challenging a requirement, explaining a trade-off or finding a simpler way to achieve the same thing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Most of our web work is built around TypeScript, React and Next.js, alongside APIs, cloud services, headless platforms and other backend technologies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write production code across the stack and stay involved in the day-to-day engineering work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take the lead on technical decisions within the team, bringing in principal engineers and others when decisions have wider implications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help turn large or difficult problems into work the team can understand and deliver.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Line manage 3–4 engineers through regular 1:1s, feedback, coaching and career conversations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review code, talk through designs and help engineers make good technical decisions rather than simply making those decisions for them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with delivery, design, product and client teams to understand what we’re trying to achieve and find an appropriate technical approach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep an eye on the things that make software good to work with and reliable in production: testing, CI/CD, observability, security, accessibility and performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help design and evolve web platforms that integrate with APIs, headless systems and third-party services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the wider engineering team at Code, sharing what works, challenging what doesn’t and helping us improve how we build software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve probably already worked as a senior or lead engineer in a team building and shipping software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re comfortable taking responsibility for technical decisions, but you also know when a decision needs wider discussion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ll need strong hands-on TypeScript experience and good experience with modern web development using React, Next.js or similar frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You should also be comfortable working beyond the frontend. That might mean Node.js, C#/.NET or another server-side technology. We care more about your ability to understand APIs, backend services and how the whole system fits together than whether your experience exactly matches our stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We’d also expect you to be comfortable with many of the things that come with building modern web platforms: APIs, server-side rendering, automated testing, CI/CD, cloud services, web performance and integrating with third-party or headless systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ll need to be able to explain technical ideas clearly. Some conversations will be with engineers; others will be with designers, delivery people, clients or stakeholders who don’t particularly care how the codeworks. Being able to adjust how you communicate matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience line managing engineers is useful, but it isn’t essential if you’ve already spent time mentoring, coaching and supporting other developers and want to take on that responsibility formally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We don’t expect you to know everything. Experience with Azure, AWS or GCP is useful, as is experience across both TypeScript and C#/.NET, but neither is a requirement. We’re more interested in good engineering judgement, curiosity and someone who can help a team make sensible decisions and ship good software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Life at WPP Media &amp;amp; Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our passion for shaping the next era of media is powered by our commitment to&amp;nbsp;Be Extraordinary, investing in our employees to inspire transformational creativity. We also&amp;nbsp;Lead Optimistically,&amp;nbsp;firmly believing&amp;nbsp;in and&amp;nbsp;Championing Growth and Development&amp;nbsp;for every individual. This commitment allows WPP Media employees to&amp;nbsp;leverage&amp;nbsp;the extensive global WPP Media &amp;amp; WPP networks to pursue their passions, build vital professional connections, and learn at the&amp;nbsp;cutting edge&amp;nbsp;of marketing and advertising.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&amp;nbsp;Create an Open environment&amp;nbsp;built on trust and respect, where everyone feels they belong and has opportunities to progress. This inclusive culture is fostered through a variety of employee resource groups and frequent in-office events&amp;nbsp;showcasing&amp;nbsp;team wins, sharing thought leadership, and celebrating holidays and milestone events. Our comprehensive benefits package reflects this commitment, including competitive medical, group retirement plans, vision, and dental insurance, significant paid time off, preferential partner discounts, and employee mental health awareness days.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;WPP Media is an equal opportunity employer and considers applicants for all positions without discrimination or regard to characteristics. We believe the best work happens when&amp;nbsp;we&#39;re&amp;nbsp;together, fostering creativity, collaboration, and connection in this open and supportive environment.&amp;nbsp;That&#39;s&amp;nbsp;why&amp;nbsp;we’ve&amp;nbsp;adopted a hybrid approach, with teams in the office around four days a week. If you&amp;nbsp;require&amp;nbsp;accommodations or flexibility, please discuss this with the hiring team during the interview process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Please note this is a UK based role and requires individuals to have the right to work in this location&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please read our Privacy Notice (&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.wppmedia.com/pages/privacy-policy&quot;&gt;https://www.wppmedia.com/pages/privacy-policy)&lt;/a&gt; for more information on how we process the information you provide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While we appreciate all applications received, only those candidates selected for an interview will be contacted.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Promoted&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
